{
  "track": "es",
  "level": "A1",
  "unit": 50,
  "title": "Every day",
  "description": "Name the jobs you do at home, and say when you do them.",
  "explanation": {
    "summary": "The last unit of A1 is a set of -ar verbs: the things you do around the house. It is a good place to finish, because everything here is a verb you can use straight away.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "The verbs",
        "body": "Barrer, planchar, lavar, doblar, fregar, cortar, nadar, pescar, pasear and visitar are all regular -ar verbs. You drop the -ar and add the ending of the person: yo barro, tú barres, él barre.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "barro la cocina",
            "en": "I sweep the kitchen"
          },
          {
            "es": "ella nada en el lago",
            "en": "she swims in the lake"
          },
          {
            "es": "visitamos a mi abuela",
            "en": "we visit my grandmother"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Every day",
        "body": "These verbs take a thing, and the thing keeps its article: barro el suelo, lavo los platos, doblo la ropa. The word for the floor is el suelo, and the word for the washing is la ropa.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "lavo la ropa",
            "en": "I wash the clothes"
          },
          {
            "es": "doblo la ropa",
            "en": "I fold the clothes"
          },
          {
            "es": "corto el pan",
            "en": "I cut the bread"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
